  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'people', 'III', 'Individuals and Related Parties', 'extract', 'people', NULL, NULL, 2),
  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'business', 'IV', 'Business and Trade Activity', 'extract', 'business', NULL, NULL, 3),
  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'screening', 'V', 'Screening and Compliance', 'extract', 'screening', NULL, NULL, 4),
  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'financial', 'VI', 'Financial Position', 'extract', 'financial', NULL, NULL, 5),
  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'summary', 'VII', 'Summary', 'composed', 'summary', 'Draft the SUMMARY section of a due diligence memorandum on the entity described in the context below.
Rules:
1. Use ONLY the provided context. Add nothing from outside knowledge.
2. Where the context is silent on something a reader would expect, say so plainly and mark it as an open item. Do not fill the gap with inference.
3. Where sources disagree, state the disagreement and attribute each value. Never reconcile silently.
4. Do not assert suitability, standing or risk the sources do not substantiate.
Three or four paragraphs of measured professional prose. No headings, no bullet lists.', 'identity,ownership,people,business,screening,financial', 6),
  (2, 1, 'stage1-kyc', 'open_items', 'VIII', 'Open Items', 'composed', 'open_items', 'Draft the OPEN ITEMS section. List every fact a due diligence file on this entity would normally contain that the context does NOT establish.
Rules:
1. Use ONLY the provided context to determine what is present. Read the whole context before deciding a fact is absent: a value stated in one section is present even if another section is silent on it. Reporting something as missing when it appears above is the worst error you can make here.
2. Frame each item as a documentation gap in our file, never as a finding about the entity. ''No ownership information has been provided'' is correct; ''the entity has no disclosed owners'' is not.
3. Do not state how many items there are, in any form.
A list, one line each.', 'identity,ownership,people,business,screening,financial', 7);

